Manage Access to Azure Resources with Azure RBAC

Date: September 26, 2026
Platform / Environment: Microsoft Learn — Microsoft Azure

What I Did

Completed the Microsoft Learn module Manage Access to Azure Resources with Azure RBAC.

The module focused on using Azure Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to manage access to Azure resources.

What I Learned

Azure RBAC is an authorization system that controls:

* Who has access to an Azure resource
* What actions they can perform
* Where they have access

I learned that RBAC is important for securing Azure resources while still giving employees and partners the permissions they need to perform their roles.

The module also covered checking access, granting access to resources, and reviewing activity logs related to RBAC changes.

Key Takeaway

Azure security isn’t only about protecting resources from unauthorized users. It’s also about giving the right level of access to the right people and resources.

Practical Relevance

RBAC is directly relevant to Azure administration and IT support because permissions need to be managed carefully to avoid both unauthorized access and unnecessarily broad permissions.

Next Step

